WEBVTT

00:45.087 --> 00:48.048
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:48.674 --> 00:50.884
Ending The Chef's Path.

00:50.968 --> 00:53.303
THE CHEF'S PATH HAS ENDED

01:05.941 --> 01:08.026
Communications Security.
This is First Lieutenant Cho Ye-rin.

01:10.070 --> 01:11.071
What?

01:13.365 --> 01:16.201
EPISODE 3

01:19.621 --> 01:20.622
Seriously?

01:20.706 --> 01:23.584
I can't believe I have to
be on duty on a day like today.

01:24.084 --> 01:25.460
What can we do

01:25.544 --> 01:27.462
when guys like Kang Seong-jae
gobble up the junior T.O.?

01:27.546 --> 01:30.132
When he's done in the mess hall,
you put him on duty.

01:30.215 --> 01:32.301
We need to work him so hard
he won't know what hit him.

01:32.384 --> 01:33.677
He's just whining
because it's too easy for him.

01:33.760 --> 01:34.761
Don't you worry.

01:34.845 --> 01:36.888
Unlike somebody,
I don't coddle my subordinates.

01:36.972 --> 01:38.140
I'm counting on it.

01:41.768 --> 01:42.853
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

01:43.729 --> 01:45.314
Didn't you hear that?

01:45.397 --> 01:46.481
What sound?

01:46.565 --> 01:48.358
All I hear are the waves crashing.

01:48.442 --> 01:49.776
Now, come on.

02:01.038 --> 02:02.247
Help me.

02:05.334 --> 02:06.335
COMPANY COMMANDER'S OFFICE

02:07.753 --> 02:08.754
Salute.

02:10.422 --> 02:11.840
Goodness, what in the world?

02:12.174 --> 02:13.383
What's all this commotion, huh?

02:13.467 --> 02:14.926
What in the world is going on?

02:15.010 --> 02:16.762
Didn't I say some guys have all the luck?

02:18.221 --> 02:20.849
How could a jackpot like this
just fall into our laps right now?

02:20.932 --> 02:22.893
This isn't a jackpot.
It's a massive headache.

02:23.477 --> 02:26.313
To be blunt, we have no idea
what he was thinking coming down here.

02:26.396 --> 02:28.565
He breached our perimeter.

02:28.857 --> 02:31.109
A slip-up and we're all disciplined.

02:31.401 --> 02:32.402
Come on.

02:32.486 --> 02:34.029
Let's look on the bright side.

02:34.112 --> 02:35.364
The man from the North

02:35.447 --> 02:37.324
risked it all to come here and defect

02:37.407 --> 02:39.576
and all we did was rescue him.

02:48.752 --> 02:49.753
Hey.

02:50.712 --> 02:51.713
Come on.

02:51.963 --> 02:53.965
So, how'd you end up all the way out here?

02:55.175 --> 02:56.718
It'll all come out
in the investigation anyway.

02:56.802 --> 02:58.679
So don't bother making up
some strange story.

03:01.515 --> 03:02.641
It...

03:03.558 --> 03:04.976
It was just an accident.

03:05.602 --> 03:06.603
An accident?

03:06.895 --> 03:07.979
The weather was awful.

03:12.567 --> 03:14.486
I was completely disoriented.

03:16.863 --> 03:18.657
When I finally came to...

03:20.617 --> 03:22.744
how was I to know this was South Joseon?

03:26.123 --> 03:27.457
Well, this is...

03:33.213 --> 03:34.589
Sir, hello.

03:35.841 --> 03:37.884
I'm Captain Hwang Seok-ho.

03:38.343 --> 03:39.928
If there's anything you need

03:40.137 --> 03:41.388
please don't hesitate to tell me.

03:44.349 --> 03:45.642
Get some blankets from the supply room.

03:46.017 --> 03:47.561
Just grab everything we have.

03:48.103 --> 03:49.104
Yes, sir!

03:54.568 --> 03:56.069
Don't try any tricks.

03:56.486 --> 03:57.529
Just send me back.

03:58.905 --> 04:01.992
Sir, why would you say something so harsh?

04:02.743 --> 04:04.661
Didn't I tell you it was just an accident?

04:06.621 --> 04:08.206
Back to the Republic.

04:08.290 --> 04:10.125
I'm telling you to quickly send me back.

04:10.417 --> 04:13.336
Now, sir, let's not be too hasty.

04:13.587 --> 04:15.172
Take your time and think it over.

04:15.630 --> 04:17.257
This may have happened by accident

04:17.466 --> 04:20.218
but you have a rare opportunity
to change your life.

04:20.677 --> 04:23.013
Others risk their lives to cross
even as we speak.

04:23.096 --> 04:24.973
No place is warmer

04:25.348 --> 04:27.517
than the embrace of our Supreme Leader.

04:31.229 --> 04:32.939
- Now, listen...
- I'm not interested.

04:33.023 --> 04:34.691
Call the Republic.

04:34.941 --> 04:35.942
I said I want to go back.

04:36.026 --> 04:38.195
- Sir...
- Right, you want to go back now?

04:38.278 --> 04:41.490
Mister, to hear you talk,
you'd think you missed your stop.

04:41.740 --> 04:43.950
This isn't such a simple matter, you know?

04:44.242 --> 04:46.620
To you, it may be as simple as saying
you want to go back

04:46.787 --> 04:49.039
but if something goes wrong

04:49.122 --> 04:51.625
- it's our heads that will roll.
- Master Sergeant.

04:51.833 --> 04:53.460
Can I have a word with you?

04:56.546 --> 04:57.547
I mean...

04:58.048 --> 04:59.883
- You can come in.
- Am I wrong?

05:00.550 --> 05:01.760
Master Sergeant.

05:01.843 --> 05:04.304
Why do you have to be
so unhelpful? Just why?

05:04.387 --> 05:06.097
What? Can't I be suspicious?

05:06.181 --> 05:07.849
He might have some hidden agenda.

05:07.933 --> 05:09.434
If we send him back to the North now

05:09.518 --> 05:11.311
the fallout is going to land on us.

05:11.686 --> 05:13.939
Please, stop looking at
what's right in front of you.

05:14.064 --> 05:16.650
How are we supposed to stop a man
asking to see the Supreme Leader?

05:16.900 --> 05:19.986
Company Commander,
please stop talking nonsense.

05:21.238 --> 05:22.989
Aren't you the one being reckless,
MasterSergeant?

05:24.199 --> 05:26.201
I know your military career
is a dead end, but still.

05:26.409 --> 05:28.703
What did you say?
I've been letting this slide

05:28.787 --> 05:29.788
but who do you think you are?

05:29.871 --> 05:31.832
Would you two just stop it, seriously!

05:32.499 --> 05:35.252
- This is not the time to fight.
- Unbelievable.

05:35.836 --> 05:39.297
Like the Master Sergeant said,
we just need to verify his identity.

05:39.506 --> 05:42.050
He says he won't defect

05:42.133 --> 05:43.927
but the situation was so sudden

05:44.010 --> 05:45.595
so let's not intimidate him.

05:45.679 --> 05:46.888
Let's be calm

05:47.180 --> 05:49.850
and talk this through, shall we?

05:50.600 --> 05:51.601
Okay?

05:52.227 --> 05:54.563
A Master Sergeant should think about
turning a crisis into an advantage.

05:54.646 --> 05:57.065
What's going to happen
if you keep saying it can't be done?

05:57.148 --> 06:00.735
Please. If words could cross the 38th
we'd have been reunified long ago.

06:00.819 --> 06:01.903
Jeez...

06:02.904 --> 06:04.614
If you two just stay here

06:04.698 --> 06:06.366
I'll go in and talk to him.

06:09.286 --> 06:10.287
That's right.

06:10.370 --> 06:11.955
Cho Ye-rin, you give it a try.

06:14.499 --> 06:15.709
- Okay.
- Go.

06:17.419 --> 06:18.503
You must be cold.

06:18.587 --> 06:19.963
Have something warm to drink.

06:29.306 --> 06:30.599
What is this?

06:31.933 --> 06:33.101
Is it not to your liking?

06:36.730 --> 06:39.107
I'm a man who just barely
escaped with his life.

06:40.609 --> 06:42.444
With this warm honey tea

06:43.194 --> 06:44.779
did you think you could sway my heart?

06:45.780 --> 06:46.865
What do you take me for?

06:47.657 --> 06:48.950
No, that's not it at all.

06:49.034 --> 06:50.118
If there's anything you need

06:50.201 --> 06:51.620
please feel free to tell me.

06:52.787 --> 06:54.414
Promise me.

06:55.290 --> 06:56.875
That here, in this South Joseon

06:57.375 --> 06:59.210
I did not drink even a sip of water.

06:59.294 --> 07:00.754
You will relay that to the Republic.

07:02.839 --> 07:04.841
Yes, I understand.

07:04.925 --> 07:08.303
I will make sure no harm comes to you.

07:08.386 --> 07:09.471
Of course you will.

07:22.776 --> 07:23.818
You must be very hungry, right?

07:23.902 --> 07:25.695
Didn't I say I wouldn't
even drink a sip of water?

07:25.779 --> 07:27.822
You came all this way
through the wind and rain

07:28.031 --> 07:29.741
and we were being very inconsiderate.

07:30.742 --> 07:32.577
Didn't I say that I don't need anything?

07:39.584 --> 07:41.294
What did he say?
Does he want to stay here?

07:41.670 --> 07:43.254
He's asking to be sent back to the North.

07:44.172 --> 07:47.008
I'm telling you,
we're all dead if he goes back.

07:47.092 --> 07:48.468
Come on, his request is ridiculous.

07:48.551 --> 07:51.930
All his family is probably up north,
so why would he settle down here?

07:53.348 --> 07:55.850
We have to change his mind before
the Regimental Commander comes.

07:56.267 --> 07:58.186
It seems like he's very hungry.

07:58.269 --> 07:59.270
Should we get him something to eat?

07:59.354 --> 08:02.107
My, my, how generous. So very generous.

08:02.315 --> 08:04.359
While we're busy feeding that guy,
I'm about to lose my own job.

08:05.151 --> 08:07.237
That's right.
An army marches on its stomach.

08:18.873 --> 08:20.625
Hey, what is all this?

08:20.792 --> 08:22.502
In the Republic of Korea

08:22.585 --> 08:25.046
you can get any food, 24/7 with this.

08:25.171 --> 08:26.798
And enjoy it to your heart's content.

08:27.132 --> 08:28.133
So...

08:28.258 --> 08:29.467
did you prepared all this

08:29.551 --> 08:31.886
to tempt me?

08:32.512 --> 08:35.223
Sir, why would you say something
so disheartening?

08:35.557 --> 08:36.975
We're not trying to tempt you.

08:37.058 --> 08:39.644
This is just how we treat our guests here.

08:40.687 --> 08:43.523
I see. So this is how
you treat guests here.

08:44.399 --> 08:45.400
Pardon?

08:46.192 --> 08:47.861
Is something missing?

08:47.944 --> 08:51.156
Are you trying to impress me
with food that someone else made?

08:51.364 --> 08:52.365
Get it all out of here.

08:53.950 --> 08:55.535
I knew it. Good grief.

08:55.785 --> 08:57.287
Get out, quickly!

08:58.997 --> 09:00.665
Unbelievable.
He won't even eat the sashimi.

09:03.626 --> 09:04.794
Kang Seong-jae.

09:04.878 --> 09:06.546
I told you to just do enough
and go inside.

09:07.380 --> 09:09.799
No, sir. I'll finish up properly
and then go.

09:12.886 --> 09:16.097
We used fresh, warm eggs from the henhouse

09:16.514 --> 09:19.059
and fried it with care
using high-quality pork

09:19.809 --> 09:22.103
only for it to end up in the trash
after all that fuss?

09:22.854 --> 09:23.897
Oh, man.

09:24.147 --> 09:25.482
That looks damn good.

09:34.574 --> 09:36.242
Communications Security!

09:36.326 --> 09:38.995
This is Private Kang Seong-jae,
mess hall. How can I...

09:41.372 --> 09:42.499
I'm sorry, can you repeat that?

09:50.006 --> 09:51.049
I didn't eat it.

09:58.306 --> 09:59.808
We just fried this fresh for you.

09:59.891 --> 10:01.601
- Please enjoy.
- Unbelievable.

10:01.976 --> 10:04.979
He refused sashimi,
which you can't even find in North Korea.

10:05.063 --> 10:07.816
So I doubt he'll be impressed
by a pork cutlet from Kang Seong-jae.

10:07.941 --> 10:08.983
Master Sergeant.

10:09.192 --> 10:10.443
Tteok-Sun-Twi!

10:10.985 --> 10:12.362
We're missing tteokbokki,
sundae, and fried snacks

10:13.029 --> 10:14.322
Both of you, please step out.

10:14.405 --> 10:15.532
Kang Seong-jae, come on.

10:15.615 --> 10:16.616
Yes, sir.

10:20.954 --> 10:22.247
What are you doing?

10:25.041 --> 10:26.793
This is our first time
hosting a guest from the North.

10:26.876 --> 10:27.877
So I apologize.

10:28.419 --> 10:32.132
As you requested,
we prepared another meal with care.

10:35.593 --> 10:36.594
I don't want it.

10:37.011 --> 10:38.012
I promise.

10:38.096 --> 10:39.889
This will not cause you any trouble.

10:41.057 --> 10:42.267
We're all just...

10:42.559 --> 10:44.144
trying to make a living.

10:44.936 --> 10:47.105
Even if you do end up
returning to the North

10:47.230 --> 10:49.357
do you think I'll hold it over you
that I treated you to a meal?

10:50.567 --> 10:51.568
So please.

10:51.651 --> 10:53.361
Just eat first.

10:55.363 --> 10:56.573
Just because you're doing this...

10:57.240 --> 10:58.950
do you think I'm going to change my mind?

11:13.047 --> 11:15.508
By the way, what kind of
fried dish is this?

11:16.134 --> 11:17.135
It's called pork cutlet.

11:17.218 --> 11:19.387
It's a dish made of
thinly pounded, fried pork.

11:19.637 --> 11:20.638
Pork cutlet?

11:22.765 --> 11:24.475
What a fancy name.

11:41.451 --> 11:42.452
Promise me.

11:43.620 --> 11:44.621
I...

11:45.496 --> 11:47.081
didn't eat anything.

11:49.042 --> 11:50.710
Yes, I promise.

12:05.850 --> 12:12.857
SOUTH JOSEON PORK CUTLET

12:15.777 --> 12:17.695
Crispy pork cutlet

12:17.779 --> 12:19.656
South Joseon pork cutlet

12:19.739 --> 12:21.532
It's so big that

12:21.616 --> 12:23.493
I can't finish it

12:23.701 --> 12:25.286
Wahoo

12:25.703 --> 12:27.538
Cutlet! Cutlet!

12:27.705 --> 12:29.457
Port cutlet!

12:29.666 --> 12:33.044
It's so, so good

12:33.628 --> 12:35.630
I can't finish it

12:36.381 --> 12:37.632
So is this...

12:37.715 --> 12:40.635
the true taste of Yankee capitalism?

12:42.845 --> 12:43.846
Let's go!

12:52.855 --> 12:54.440
Crispy and delicious

12:54.649 --> 12:56.317
South Joseon pork cutlet

12:56.401 --> 12:58.111
My nostrils and tongue

12:58.194 --> 12:59.570
Are in heaven

13:01.614 --> 13:03.157
Cutlet! Cutlet!

13:03.366 --> 13:04.867
Pork cutlet!

13:04.993 --> 13:08.288
It's so, so good

13:08.496 --> 13:10.957
It's so delicious

13:12.041 --> 13:13.626
It's as big as a pumpkin

13:13.793 --> 13:15.420
South Joseon pork cutlet

13:15.503 --> 13:17.171
The general

13:17.255 --> 13:18.965
Ate it all by himself

13:20.800 --> 13:22.385
Cutlet! Cutlet!

13:22.468 --> 13:24.512
Pork cutlet!

13:28.641 --> 13:29.642
- What?
- What?

13:29.726 --> 13:31.311
Didn't someone just sing?

13:31.853 --> 13:34.022
- Did it kill him?
- Master Sergeant.

13:34.314 --> 13:35.315
I'll go in.

13:35.398 --> 13:37.108
No, I have to go in with you.
I'm curious too.

13:37.191 --> 13:38.985
Master Sergeant,
I'm the Company Commander.

13:39.193 --> 13:41.237
- Wow, that's a cheap shot.
- Deputy Outpost Commander.

13:41.321 --> 13:43.406
- Yeah.
- How much leave do we get for this?

13:43.614 --> 13:46.659
Let's see. Last time at the GOP,
with the Division Commander's award

13:46.743 --> 13:48.202
it was a 30-day leave, wasn't it?

13:51.497 --> 13:52.582
This is a huge problem.

13:52.665 --> 13:54.042
If I'm on leave for a whole month

13:54.125 --> 13:56.044
it'll leave a huge hole
in our national defense.

13:56.127 --> 13:57.754
You guys, I'm telling you,
this is nothing to celebrate.

13:57.837 --> 13:59.630
He's raising hell,
demanding to be sent back North.

14:00.590 --> 14:01.716
Back to your places!

14:02.592 --> 14:03.885
Salute!

14:04.927 --> 14:07.180
- Where is he?
- He's safe in my office.

14:07.263 --> 14:08.723
Did you hear why he came down?

14:08.806 --> 14:10.183
It seems there was an accident.

14:10.266 --> 14:11.851
He's asking to be sent back

14:11.934 --> 14:14.062
but I think he's just saying that
because he's scared.

14:14.354 --> 14:16.731
Are you sure?
Lying to me will make things worse.

14:16.814 --> 14:19.067
It's best if you go inside
and see his state for yourselves...

14:21.319 --> 14:22.445
You punk.

14:22.528 --> 14:23.821
It's not the old times anymore.

14:23.905 --> 14:25.198
I told you to handle him with care

14:25.281 --> 14:26.407
so what are you doing in there?

14:26.491 --> 14:27.492
No, it's...

14:31.120 --> 14:32.789
- You son of a bitch.
- Let's go.

14:40.088 --> 14:41.464
Sir, are you all right?

14:41.756 --> 14:42.757
Cho Ye-rin.

14:42.840 --> 14:43.841
What did you do?

14:44.425 --> 14:45.551
He seemed hungry

14:45.635 --> 14:47.178
so I just gave him some pork cutlet.

14:47.804 --> 14:49.847
- What? Pork Cutlet?
- Yes.

14:55.520 --> 14:56.521
I...

14:57.688 --> 14:59.148
had a dream.

15:01.818 --> 15:04.487
Jeez, it's too noisy.
I can't listen to this.

15:04.570 --> 15:05.738
So the kids in South Joseon

15:05.822 --> 15:07.698
listen to this kind of garbage?

15:07.782 --> 15:11.327
No wonder they're all brainwashed
by the Yankees.

15:11.411 --> 15:12.703
I'm wondering

15:12.787 --> 15:14.372
what all the fuss is about

15:14.455 --> 15:16.290
so let me have a listen.

15:16.707 --> 15:18.709
Hey, my ears are bleeding.

15:36.811 --> 15:38.604
My lips denied it

15:39.105 --> 15:41.190
but my body could not lie.

15:50.324 --> 15:51.617
In that moment

15:52.910 --> 15:54.579
I knew I had to do it!

15:55.329 --> 15:57.248
To become a singer for freedom.

15:57.498 --> 16:00.293
A rocker of the people!

16:04.881 --> 16:05.882
A rocker?

16:11.762 --> 16:12.930
And today...

16:14.390 --> 16:16.934
I've had a taste of freedom here.

16:17.643 --> 16:18.686
The taste of freedom...

16:19.270 --> 16:21.314
was so savory

16:21.606 --> 16:22.815
crispy...

16:24.275 --> 16:25.735
rich...

16:26.569 --> 16:29.655
and absolutely blissful.

16:34.368 --> 16:35.786
A savory...

16:36.120 --> 16:38.498
and crispy freedom awaits you

16:38.581 --> 16:40.124
in the Republic of Korea.

16:40.208 --> 16:41.792
We sincerely welcome you.

16:42.126 --> 16:44.545
Even more delicious foods

16:44.629 --> 16:46.047
will be waiting for you.

16:46.297 --> 16:48.257
Republic of Korea!

16:50.009 --> 16:51.719
- Republic of Korea!
- Republic of Korea!

16:53.513 --> 16:55.348
- Republic of Korea!
- Republic of Korea!

16:57.099 --> 16:58.768
- Republic of Korea!
- Republic of Korea!

17:00.603 --> 17:01.604
Republic of...

17:12.448 --> 17:13.533
Lady comrade.

17:13.950 --> 17:14.951
Yes?

17:17.245 --> 17:18.788
That pork cutlet from earlier...

17:20.122 --> 17:22.542
did you make it yourself?

17:23.417 --> 17:24.418
No.

17:24.502 --> 17:25.545
The cook from our unit

17:25.628 --> 17:27.296
Private Kang Seong-jae, made it.

17:28.839 --> 17:29.840
Kang Seong-jae?

17:31.300 --> 17:32.301
Who's Kang Seong-jae?

17:34.303 --> 17:35.304
Private Kang Seong-jae!

17:35.555 --> 17:36.639
What's your name?

17:37.598 --> 17:39.141
Introductions, at a time like this?

17:42.019 --> 17:43.062
I'm sorry, I didn't catch that.

17:47.900 --> 17:48.901
I'm...

17:49.318 --> 17:50.695
Kim Min-ho. After coming to South Korea

17:52.488 --> 17:55.491
I've had the most
delicious meal of my life.

18:00.329 --> 18:01.664
I'm truly grateful.

18:05.960 --> 18:07.587
Private Kang Seong-jae. Thank you.

18:19.181 --> 18:21.350
Good work, everyone. I know it's late.

18:21.559 --> 18:23.269
Thanks to the efforts
of our Ourpost members

18:23.728 --> 18:25.313
we successfully handled a defection.

18:30.693 --> 18:32.153
The moment we let down our guard

18:32.236 --> 18:33.946
the Republic of Korea is at risk.

18:35.615 --> 18:36.616
Regimental Commander.

18:36.824 --> 18:38.784
As the Company Commander,
it's something I always emphasize

18:38.951 --> 18:41.245
so I believe that's why
my orders were followed so well.

18:41.329 --> 18:43.164
But I heard he walked right up
to the outpost himself?

18:44.540 --> 18:45.583
Technically...

18:45.666 --> 18:47.877
didn't we lure him in
with the pork cutlet?

18:48.419 --> 18:50.463
Right. The Master Sergeant's got a point.

18:51.297 --> 18:52.298
Who...

18:52.381 --> 18:54.550
was the soldier that made the pork cutlet?

18:54.800 --> 18:55.801
Where's Kang Seong-jae?

18:56.135 --> 18:57.678
- Private Kang Seong-jae!
- Okay, step forward.

18:57.803 --> 18:58.804
Yes, sir.

19:00.973 --> 19:02.391
This is the one.

19:02.475 --> 19:04.143
The one who made the seaweed soup

19:04.226 --> 19:05.645
that almost killed me.

19:06.979 --> 19:09.774
So this guy's a dangerous one.

19:10.441 --> 19:12.818
At this rate,
he might cause a major incident.

19:13.402 --> 19:14.862
Private Kang Seong-jae. I apologize, sir.

19:17.531 --> 19:18.866
It's all right.

19:18.949 --> 19:20.785
When you try to do great things,
mistakes can happen.

19:21.661 --> 19:24.997
But how did you make a pork cutlet
that convinced a man to defect?

19:28.334 --> 19:30.002
I just made it with all my heart

19:30.294 --> 19:32.630
hoping my sincerity would be understood.

19:34.256 --> 19:35.257
What is he talking about?

19:35.841 --> 19:36.842
Well...

19:36.926 --> 19:38.803
before Private Kang Seong-jae's transfer

19:38.886 --> 19:41.305
he wanted the Company Commander
to try his pork cutlet

19:41.389 --> 19:42.390
so he prepared that.

19:42.765 --> 19:43.891
Why is he being transferred?

19:44.684 --> 19:46.894
I'm sure I told you
not to come down so hard on your men.

19:47.895 --> 19:50.106
Where were you trying to send
such a talented soldier?

19:50.189 --> 19:51.982
Master Sergeant,
you've been watching him, right?

19:52.441 --> 19:53.901
Yes, sir. Well...

19:54.527 --> 19:57.363
He's still a private, so he's a bit green.

19:57.446 --> 19:59.615
But from what I saw today,
he's got what it takes.

19:59.699 --> 20:03.160
No, for a private, he's outstanding.

20:03.244 --> 20:06.580
- Then I'll keep him on mess duty.
- Good.

20:07.081 --> 20:08.165
Congratulations.

20:08.666 --> 20:11.252
You have completed the Hidden Quest:
Chain of Command.

20:12.002 --> 20:14.171
Just how good could it possibly be?

20:14.255 --> 20:16.590
Feel free to stop by for a meal
anytime, sir.

20:16.674 --> 20:17.717
LIKEABILITY

20:17.800 --> 20:18.801
Would that be okay?

20:18.884 --> 20:21.554
Hero, the Chef's Path restarts.

20:21.637 --> 20:22.888
THE CHEF'S PATH
RELOAD

20:23.389 --> 20:25.391
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- Private Kang Seong-jae!

20:25.474 --> 20:27.017
The Regimental Commander
asked you a question.

20:27.727 --> 20:29.395
What did you...

20:29.478 --> 20:30.938
Could I try it next time?

20:31.021 --> 20:32.022
The Pork Cutlet, I mean.

20:32.940 --> 20:35.401
Yes, I'll fry you lots and lots.

20:35.484 --> 20:37.611
- Lots and lots?
- Yes, lots and lots.

20:40.030 --> 20:41.907
I can't just let this go unrewarded.

20:42.408 --> 20:43.659
Your thoughts, Company Commander?

20:43.743 --> 20:44.827
What are you referring to, sir?

20:45.035 --> 20:46.328
A reward.

20:46.412 --> 20:48.914
As Company Commander,
can't you grant a four-day leave?

20:50.332 --> 20:51.459
There are two people

20:51.542 --> 20:52.793
on kitchen duty, right?

20:52.877 --> 20:54.253
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun!

20:55.212 --> 20:57.131
I will arrange for their reward
immediately, sir.

20:57.214 --> 20:58.924
Regimental Commander, I love you, sir!

21:00.468 --> 21:01.969
- I... I love you, sir.
- All right.

21:02.386 --> 21:03.471
I love you guys too.

21:03.929 --> 21:05.514
You've all been through a lot

21:06.182 --> 21:07.475
so go get some rest.

21:08.058 --> 21:09.143
Company, attention!

21:10.352 --> 21:12.021
Salute the Regimental Commander.

21:12.104 --> 21:13.314
Salute!

21:14.565 --> 21:15.566
Salute!

21:15.691 --> 21:16.776
Salute!

21:19.320 --> 21:20.446
At ease!

21:21.947 --> 21:22.948
What was that?

21:23.324 --> 21:25.701
We're the ones who found him,
and they don't even say a word to us?

21:25.951 --> 21:27.620
Are they seriously just leaving like this?

21:28.204 --> 21:29.413
Without giving us anything.

21:29.747 --> 21:33.542
At this rate, maybe we should've
just fried him a pork cutlet too.

21:35.377 --> 21:38.088
That punk's really getting on my nerves.

21:44.720 --> 21:45.721
At ease.

21:49.308 --> 21:50.810
Man, Seok-ho.

21:50.893 --> 21:52.895
Your luck is just incredible.

21:53.479 --> 21:55.397
You know if this had gone south,
you'd face discipline, right?

21:55.940 --> 21:58.192
I believe the five-star treatment
we gave him

21:58.275 --> 22:00.027
ensuring his comfort

22:00.361 --> 22:02.613
is what ultimately led to his defection.

22:02.822 --> 22:05.032
That pork cutlet was a stroke of genius.

22:05.449 --> 22:08.327
Imagine how moving that must've been
for someone from the North.

22:08.410 --> 22:11.247
A pork cutlet, made with love

22:11.330 --> 22:12.832
placed right in front of him.

22:12.915 --> 22:14.250
Yes, sir.

22:14.333 --> 22:17.503
- That's right, sir.
- So train him well. Understood?

22:17.711 --> 22:19.171
Nothing beats an excellent cook

22:19.255 --> 22:20.673
for boosting unit morale.

22:21.215 --> 22:23.133
As you said, Battalion Commander

22:23.509 --> 22:24.844
I will train him well.

22:27.179 --> 22:30.099
It's good to see you doing fine.

22:30.182 --> 22:31.684
No trouble, I hope?

22:32.268 --> 22:33.644
No, sir. I'm fine.

22:35.187 --> 22:36.188
Good.

22:37.273 --> 22:38.649
All right, I'm heading out.

22:38.732 --> 22:40.067
Don't see me out, just stay inside.

22:40.276 --> 22:41.402
- Yes, sir.
- You all worked hard.

22:42.027 --> 22:43.028
All right, attention!

22:44.071 --> 22:45.072
I love you.

22:47.575 --> 22:48.576
Right.

22:55.207 --> 22:56.250
- Salute!
- Salute!

22:57.918 --> 22:59.879
We're lucky it all ended well.

23:00.379 --> 23:02.047
Imagine if we had sent him back
like someone suggested.

23:02.131 --> 23:04.341
We'd all be under investigation,
and it would've been a disaster.

23:04.633 --> 23:07.887
Good thing I, Hwang Seok-ho,
stepped up and showed leadership.

23:07.970 --> 23:10.014
Oh, please. Your "great leadership"?

23:10.097 --> 23:11.640
You just ordered tons of takeout.

23:11.849 --> 23:13.350
Wasn't it our Company Commander

23:13.434 --> 23:14.852
who ordered takeout for an entire army?

23:14.935 --> 23:16.562
Speaking of which, you were the one

23:16.645 --> 23:18.355
who gave up quickly, Master Sergeant.

23:18.439 --> 23:20.566
I mean, a man comes here seeking freedom

23:20.649 --> 23:22.818
and you were just going to
heartlessly send him back?

23:23.027 --> 23:24.862
Hey, that's why we fed him, isn't it?

23:24.945 --> 23:26.322
With that savory

23:26.405 --> 23:28.490
crispy taste of freedom.

23:28.574 --> 23:29.575
The pork cutlet.

23:29.658 --> 23:32.703
You know the one.
Kang Seong-jae first made it for me.

23:32.786 --> 23:34.288
If it weren't for me,

23:34.371 --> 23:35.623
that pork cutlet wouldn't even exist.

23:35.706 --> 23:36.707
Got it? Got it?

23:36.790 --> 23:37.958
Because I, Hwang Seok-ho

23:38.042 --> 23:39.585
- didn't eat that Pork Cutlet...
- Right.

23:39.960 --> 23:42.630
Since you didn't eat the pork cutlet,
Company Commander

23:42.796 --> 23:45.090
another citizen of the Republic
of Korea was born.

23:45.215 --> 23:48.761
Anyway, that Kang Seong-jae
is strange, isn't he?

23:48.844 --> 23:51.722
Everyone else tries
to get out of being a cook.

23:52.014 --> 23:54.725
He's really something else.

23:54.808 --> 23:57.770
We've never had a rookie
cause so much trouble right away.

23:59.229 --> 24:00.648
All right, let's head inside.

24:01.106 --> 24:02.107
Yes, sir.

24:02.983 --> 24:03.984
Goodness.

24:23.295 --> 24:25.172
- Private Kang Seong-jae.
- Here.

24:26.006 --> 24:27.257
Start wearing this today.

24:27.341 --> 24:30.719
KANG SEONG-JAE

24:32.805 --> 24:33.806
Thank you.

24:36.350 --> 24:37.351
Oh, wait.

24:37.977 --> 24:40.062
I'm just going to
use the restroom real quick.

24:41.230 --> 24:42.815
Don't touch anything weird.

24:42.898 --> 24:44.316
Yes, sir.

25:09.341 --> 25:11.468
Job change from Kitchen Assistant to Cook

25:11.552 --> 25:12.803
complete.

25:13.887 --> 25:16.557
New skills and recipes
have been activated.

25:26.275 --> 25:28.360
Oh, you actually look like

25:28.444 --> 25:29.695
a cook in that.

25:33.157 --> 25:34.283
What do you want to try first?

25:35.367 --> 25:36.577
I'm sorry, what was that?

25:36.660 --> 25:38.454
Well, you're a real cook now.

25:38.537 --> 25:39.997
You can't just wash dishes forever.

25:41.415 --> 25:42.875
I will do my best.

25:42.958 --> 25:45.210
Still, since it's your first day...

25:45.294 --> 25:46.837
TODAY'S MENU

25:46.920 --> 25:48.047
Let's try making this.

25:48.547 --> 25:49.882
Seasoned radish salad?

25:49.965 --> 25:51.341
That's right. Seasoned radish salad.

25:54.511 --> 25:56.555
Now that I'm a real cook

25:56.847 --> 25:58.390
shall I show them what I've got?

26:10.069 --> 26:13.363
Jeez, the way he holds that knife
is making me nervous.

26:13.947 --> 26:16.575
- Chop to the rhythm.
- Fail.

26:16.825 --> 26:19.161
- Chop to the rhythm.
- Fail.

26:21.413 --> 26:22.414
Fail.

26:22.915 --> 26:23.916
To the rhythm.

26:23.999 --> 26:26.168
Chop to the rhythm.

26:26.251 --> 26:27.586
- Fail.
- Increase proficiency

26:27.669 --> 26:28.962
to improve your knife skills.

26:29.713 --> 26:32.424
Goodness, your knife work
is painful to watch.

26:32.508 --> 26:35.052
You don't chop with brute force, okay?

26:35.135 --> 26:36.804
Relax your body

26:36.887 --> 26:39.056
and use the snap of your wrist. See?

26:39.515 --> 26:42.017
Chop, chop, chop, chop, chop.

26:42.101 --> 26:44.394
See? That's how you're supposed to do it.

26:46.188 --> 26:47.356
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun, are you okay?

26:47.898 --> 26:49.358
What? Why?

26:51.527 --> 26:52.820
I think I'm coming down with something.

26:53.821 --> 26:54.822
Hurry up and finish it.

27:06.208 --> 27:07.501
That stings.

27:10.629 --> 27:12.840
Who stopped chopping this radish halfway?

27:19.513 --> 27:21.306
Yeah, well, things happen.

27:21.390 --> 27:22.641
LEFTOVER TRAFFIC LIGHT
BAD

27:24.101 --> 27:25.102
DAY 3 SINCE JOB CHANGE

27:25.352 --> 27:26.353
Good.

27:27.229 --> 27:29.565
Good.

27:34.027 --> 27:36.905
Basic Knife Skills
proficiency has increased.

27:36.989 --> 27:38.657
PROFICIENCY: BASIC KNIFE SKILLS

27:44.997 --> 27:46.373
DAY 3 SINCE JOB CHANGE

27:47.624 --> 27:50.419
DAY 7 SINCE JOB CHANGE

27:53.505 --> 27:55.424
Why is this knife so dull?

28:45.098 --> 28:48.310
Stir-fry proficiency has increased.

28:49.269 --> 28:50.270
Much better.

29:04.076 --> 29:05.077
Well, now.

29:05.494 --> 29:07.704
What did I tell you, huh?

29:07.996 --> 29:09.414
If you can't use a knife

29:09.498 --> 29:11.375
then use a machine like this. A machine!

29:11.458 --> 29:15.003
Look how nice and neat it looks
when you use a machine.

29:15.087 --> 29:16.380
Isn't the only potato dish
we serve in the mess hall

29:16.463 --> 29:18.590
mashed potatoes?

29:18.966 --> 29:20.550
They're usually a pile of mush

29:20.634 --> 29:22.302
so seeing them in one piece is so weird.

29:25.597 --> 29:27.432
- It even tastes good.
- It's delicious.

29:33.855 --> 29:34.856
Well, I'll be.

29:44.866 --> 29:46.159
LEFTOVER TRAFFIC LIGHT

29:46.243 --> 29:48.161
DAY 7 SINCE JOB CHANGE

29:48.537 --> 29:49.538
DAY 8 SINCE JOB CHANGE

29:57.296 --> 30:00.299
Frying proficiency has increased.

30:22.529 --> 30:25.282
Seasoned salad proficiency has increased.

30:25.407 --> 30:26.616
Attention!

30:26.700 --> 30:27.784
Roll call is over.

30:28.452 --> 30:30.662
Don't even think about passing out
just because you're sleepy.

30:30.746 --> 30:32.914
And that goes for you punks
who skip meals if you're not hungry.

30:35.917 --> 30:37.252
Why isn't he here?

30:40.756 --> 30:41.757
Where are you headed?

30:42.007 --> 30:43.258
- Enjoy your meal, sir.
- Where are you going?

30:43.342 --> 30:44.343
GANGLIM OUTPOST

30:44.426 --> 30:46.053
LEFTOVER FOOD SIGNAL
GOOD

30:52.517 --> 30:54.269
If we don't get any leftovers

30:54.353 --> 30:56.480
how are we supposed to feed the pigs?

30:56.980 --> 31:00.442
The kids are eating well these days.
They're scraping their plates clean.

31:00.525 --> 31:01.985
I'm telling you,
you don't even need to do the dishes.

31:02.569 --> 31:04.780
Thanks to you,
the pork cutlets came out great.

31:04.863 --> 31:05.864
Thank you.

31:06.990 --> 31:07.991
So...

31:08.658 --> 31:10.827
Did I help at all?

31:11.119 --> 31:13.246
Yes, you were a huge help.

31:13.705 --> 31:16.166
Would you believe that a pork cutlet,
made with pork from Miss Jung's

31:16.500 --> 31:18.293
could bring someone freedom?

31:19.544 --> 31:20.545
Can you believe it?

31:22.589 --> 31:24.466
Did you eat something wrong today?

31:24.549 --> 31:27.010
What nonsense are you talking?

31:27.135 --> 31:28.678
Let me know if you need anything else.

31:32.849 --> 31:34.643
She complains of too many leftovers

31:34.726 --> 31:36.103
and when there's not enough.

31:36.686 --> 31:38.397
She only does this to me.

31:45.112 --> 31:47.989
LIKEABILITY 70%

31:49.908 --> 31:53.954
Caught in a storm,
Mr. Kim's boat drifted to South Korea.

31:55.205 --> 31:57.332
Mr. Kim didn't intend to defect

31:57.416 --> 32:00.085
but a military personnel's
kindness moved him

32:00.168 --> 32:01.461
and he changed his mind.

32:02.504 --> 32:03.505
Pork cutlet.

32:04.840 --> 32:06.383
It's the pork cutlet guy.

32:06.925 --> 32:08.844
I'd like to have a pork cutlet.

32:09.261 --> 32:10.887
Defense Minister Kim Tae-hwan

32:10.971 --> 32:13.390
met Colonel Bae
and Lieutenant Colonel Baek...

32:13.473 --> 32:16.143
Jeez. They met the Defense Minister

32:16.226 --> 32:18.019
and we only get a four-day vacation?

32:18.103 --> 32:21.022
All those guys care about
is getting their next star, sir.

32:21.106 --> 32:22.732
We shouldn't expect too much
from them, sir.

32:24.734 --> 32:27.737
With the threat of war looming every day

32:27.821 --> 32:30.699
this "pork cutlet defection'"shows
how we treat Northerners

32:30.782 --> 32:33.535
and is being seen
as a humanitarian solution.

32:33.910 --> 32:36.538
- Jung Min-a, Armed Forces TV.
- Hey, Kang Seong-jae!

32:36.621 --> 32:38.707
- ...on social media in remote areas...
- Seong-jae!

32:38.790 --> 32:40.542
Private Kang Seong-jae!

32:41.001 --> 32:43.211
Were you hoping for a mention on TV?

32:43.420 --> 32:44.754
No, sir.

32:44.838 --> 32:46.756
You got a reward. Isn't it enough?

32:46.840 --> 32:48.800
Yeah, right. I've never gotten one.

32:48.884 --> 32:49.885
Hey, Joo Sang-uk.

32:50.469 --> 32:51.595
Corporal Joo Sang-uk.

32:51.678 --> 32:53.972
You said you'd introduce me to a girl
during my leave.

32:54.347 --> 32:55.765
My leave is almost here.

32:55.849 --> 32:57.017
Are you just going to be all talk?

32:57.559 --> 32:59.102
What do you take me for?

32:59.186 --> 33:00.353
You really want me to set you up?

33:00.437 --> 33:02.022
Yes, right now. Give me your phone.

33:02.481 --> 33:05.317
- Whoa, hold on.
- Barracks 1, assemble! Get him!

33:05.400 --> 33:07.235
Wait, wait, wait.

33:07.486 --> 33:09.112
- Kang Seong-jae.
- Private Kang Seong-jae.

33:09.196 --> 33:10.906
...Visiting residents to check it...

33:10.989 --> 33:12.699
Hey, show me the pics. Unlock it.

33:20.665 --> 33:22.292
Military life must be easy for you.

33:22.375 --> 33:23.793
Humming to yourself like that.

33:24.920 --> 33:26.713
I'm sorry. I didn't even realize.

33:27.255 --> 33:30.050
We go easy on you, and you
walk around with a stupid grin.

33:30.258 --> 33:32.886
In Barracks 2, they'd kick your ass.

33:32.969 --> 33:34.304
You got lucky with good seniors

33:34.387 --> 33:36.056
and that's why they go this easy on you.

33:36.139 --> 33:37.182
Got it?

33:37.516 --> 33:39.559
The vibe in Barracks 2
is absolutely brutal.

33:42.562 --> 33:43.563
- Salute!
- Salute!

33:45.315 --> 33:47.567
You should be cleaning in silence.

33:47.651 --> 33:49.694
You're so loud, I get constipated

33:49.778 --> 33:51.863
just hearing how well the army runs.

33:53.990 --> 33:55.951
- Hey, TMI.
- Private Tak Mun-ik.

33:56.576 --> 33:59.037
You think making private first class
gives you the right to run your mouth off?

33:59.871 --> 34:01.831
If you act like that,
what will your privates learn from you?

34:02.249 --> 34:03.959
I'm sorry. That's not what I meant...

34:04.626 --> 34:05.919
Watch your damn mouth.

34:07.587 --> 34:08.964
Having a grand old time, aren't you?

34:10.090 --> 34:12.300
The seniors are all babying you

34:12.384 --> 34:13.677
so you think you own the place, huh?

34:14.135 --> 34:15.136
No, sir!

34:18.056 --> 34:19.766
This punk's giving me a look I don't like.

34:21.226 --> 34:22.435
Don't push your luck.

34:22.727 --> 34:25.438
Stop showing off frying pork cutlets
when no one even asked you to.

34:27.566 --> 34:30.443
Warning! Hero, please step away.

34:31.945 --> 34:33.863
What are you gonna do, you little punk?

34:36.324 --> 34:38.243
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol,
I'll make sure to straighten him out.

34:40.453 --> 34:43.206
A little rank and you boss me around?
You've gotten bold.

34:45.458 --> 34:47.252
Want a beating before your junior

34:47.335 --> 34:48.837
to get a reality check?

34:50.005 --> 34:51.172
Turn.

34:53.383 --> 34:54.551
Are you crazy?

34:55.260 --> 34:58.221
This isn't the old days.
You can't leave marks on a kid now.

34:58.471 --> 35:01.850
Your spoiling them is the problem,
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

35:01.933 --> 35:03.143
And what about you?

35:03.226 --> 35:05.353
When I was swamped and had no leave

35:05.437 --> 35:07.439
I asked for a Kitchen Assistant

35:07.522 --> 35:09.232
you just blew me off,
saying you were too busy

35:09.316 --> 35:12.193
and now you're whining your ass off
because you didn't get commended?

35:13.820 --> 35:15.030
And you little shit

35:15.113 --> 35:18.658
I can ignore it
if you punish someone for a mistake.

35:19.242 --> 35:21.453
Take it to the Regimental Commander
if you have a problem.

35:21.536 --> 35:23.330
Why take it out on an innocent kid?

35:23.413 --> 35:24.623
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

35:25.206 --> 35:27.125
Since when were you
so full of love for all mankind?

35:28.418 --> 35:29.961
Look, from what I heard

35:30.128 --> 35:32.339
it's not like you guys
found and caught him.

35:32.422 --> 35:34.132
He walked in on his own, right?

35:35.216 --> 35:36.468
That guy's got some guts.

35:36.551 --> 35:38.928
How did he bypass your security?

35:47.437 --> 35:49.564
Just focus on managing your own barracks.

35:50.023 --> 35:53.360
And stop messing with my guys
who still have a long time to serve.

35:56.655 --> 35:58.031
You two, with me.

35:58.657 --> 35:59.699
Aren't you going to watch M-Countdown?

35:59.783 --> 36:00.825
RESTROOM

36:08.500 --> 36:09.501
You know what the army is?

36:09.793 --> 36:12.754
It's a place where rumors spread
even if you just stare at a wall.

36:13.129 --> 36:15.173
Is it okay for two guys
at the bottom of the food chain

36:15.256 --> 36:16.466
to run your mouths?

36:16.675 --> 36:19.219
That punk only lays off you
because I'm here.

36:19.678 --> 36:20.679
Got it?

36:21.012 --> 36:23.348
You're not hurt or anything, are you?

36:24.099 --> 36:25.100
I'm fine, sir.

36:26.017 --> 36:27.560
- Remember this.
- Private Kang Seong-jae!

36:27.644 --> 36:28.645
Until I go on leave..

36:28.728 --> 36:30.563
I repeat. Until I go on leave

36:30.647 --> 36:32.399
don't you dare get hurt.

36:32.732 --> 36:33.817
If you get hurt...

36:34.818 --> 36:38.488
I might just turn into a beast.

36:40.490 --> 36:44.244
GANGLIM

36:52.377 --> 36:53.378
Well.

36:53.461 --> 36:55.004
Look who it is.
Someone important has arrived.

36:55.171 --> 36:56.631
What are you referring to, sir?

36:57.090 --> 36:59.259
What's the lunch menu for this Wednesday?

37:02.679 --> 37:05.223
Zucchini soybean paste stew
and steamed eggs...

37:05.306 --> 37:06.766
That's the one. That's the problem.

37:07.016 --> 37:08.977
The dreaded braised pollack.

37:10.311 --> 37:12.105
You mean the
braised boneless pollack, sir?

37:14.149 --> 37:17.736
One of the easiest ways to tell
if someone's served in the military

37:17.819 --> 37:20.155
is their take on braised pollack.

37:20.238 --> 37:21.781
In the outside world, that same dish

37:21.865 --> 37:23.867
Man, it's a delicacy
you can't get enough of.

37:24.033 --> 37:25.034
But in the army

37:25.118 --> 37:27.579
it's an item that everyone knows to skip.

37:27.912 --> 37:29.956
Our Miss Jung is going to be happy.

37:30.540 --> 37:32.292
She'll be leaving
with a full bucket of leftovers.

37:33.168 --> 37:34.294
BRAISED BONELESS POLLACK

37:36.379 --> 37:39.090
AVAILABLE RECIPE
BRAISED BONELESS POLLACK

37:48.099 --> 37:53.104
BRAISED BONELESS POLLACK
SLICE ONIONS AND STIR-FRY IN OLIVE OIL

37:53.188 --> 37:54.189
SEASON THE POLLACK WITH SALT AND PEPPER
AND ADD COOKING WINE

37:54.272 --> 37:55.940
IN AN OILED PAN OVER MEDIUM-LOW HEAT
PAN-FRY THE POLLOCK UNTIL IT'S CRISPY

37:59.110 --> 38:00.111
What are you doing?

38:01.821 --> 38:02.989
What was that just now?

38:05.116 --> 38:06.117
What do you mean, sir?

38:06.201 --> 38:07.827
You were pointing your finger around

38:07.911 --> 38:11.122
and waving it all over the place.

38:11.206 --> 38:13.208
Oh, that, sir.

38:16.211 --> 38:17.337
How many fingers do you see?

38:18.338 --> 38:19.339
Two?

38:21.341 --> 38:23.176
Okay, then how many do you see now?

38:25.762 --> 38:27.722
Seeing you go crazy like this

38:27.806 --> 38:29.933
you're adjusting well to army life.

38:30.892 --> 38:31.893
Three.

38:33.728 --> 38:34.729
What was that?

38:39.275 --> 38:41.110
Emergency! It's an emergency!

38:45.156 --> 38:46.574
Hey, guys, let's hurry.

38:46.658 --> 38:48.076
We can sort out these vests later.

38:48.159 --> 38:49.577
If it doesn't come off later,
just scrape it with a knife.

38:49.661 --> 38:50.662
Yes, sir.

38:50.745 --> 38:52.622
Scrub it clean! Leave no dust!

38:52.705 --> 38:53.706
Yes, sir.

38:53.790 --> 38:56.376
- Hurry up. Inspection is later.
- Yes, sir.

38:57.877 --> 38:59.087
Damn it.

38:59.379 --> 39:02.173
First a congressman, now
the Division Commander? What gives?

39:02.465 --> 39:05.635
There are news reports on poor meals,
so of course they're visiting, sir.

39:05.844 --> 39:06.928
But of all places, why us?

39:07.428 --> 39:09.931
Our name is Ganglim,
which means "divine descent," sir.

39:10.390 --> 39:11.516
We're living up to our name, sir.

39:11.599 --> 39:13.142
Oh, for crying out loud!

39:13.226 --> 39:14.310
BARRACKS

39:14.394 --> 39:16.396
Hey, P-Dragon. Hurry, hurry, hurry.

39:20.817 --> 39:21.818
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

39:22.068 --> 39:24.153
You need to hide your
civilian underwear, sir.

39:24.237 --> 39:25.530
The issued ones give me a rash.

39:26.030 --> 39:27.532
Hey, does anyone have a spare pair
of issued underwear?

39:27.615 --> 39:28.908
- We don't.
- None here.

39:28.992 --> 39:30.785
You guys are useless.

39:31.828 --> 39:33.121
I have a used pair.

39:33.580 --> 39:34.622
Do you want them?

39:34.706 --> 39:36.499
Are you kidding? I won't take them.

39:36.583 --> 39:37.625
Did you actually clean the mess hall?

39:37.709 --> 39:38.793
Huh? Did you?

39:39.460 --> 39:40.962
Why is it so filthy in here?

39:41.045 --> 39:44.841
This isn't a problem that
a little floor buffing will fix.

39:44.924 --> 39:48.177
This entire guard post
should've been remodeled ages ago.

39:49.304 --> 39:51.890
No matter how I look at it,
the whole setup is just awful.

39:51.973 --> 39:54.100
Should we maybe put some flowers
on the tables?

39:54.183 --> 39:55.310
Flowers, all of a sudden?

39:55.393 --> 39:56.853
Since it's just guys here

39:56.936 --> 39:59.480
we should make it look presentable, right?

39:59.564 --> 40:02.567
- But flowers...
- I heard you volunteered.

40:02.650 --> 40:04.527
That's right. Why, is there a problem?

40:04.944 --> 40:06.362
It's not that there's a problem...

40:07.447 --> 40:09.699
But the soldiers are all exhausted
from their duties, sir.

40:10.533 --> 40:12.702
You saw what happened, didn't you?
They completely snubbed our post.

40:12.785 --> 40:14.537
They were popping champagne
all by themselves.

40:14.621 --> 40:17.498
All that effort we put into
making pork cutlet was a waste.

40:18.917 --> 40:20.501
You must have been very upset, sir.

40:21.127 --> 40:22.128
Ye-rin.

40:22.295 --> 40:24.088
Upset? It's not that...

40:24.172 --> 40:25.506
He's not upset.

40:25.590 --> 40:26.716
He's just furious

40:26.799 --> 40:28.468
he was passed over for promotion again.

40:28.551 --> 40:30.678
Master Sergeant, what do you take me for?

40:30.762 --> 40:32.722
Isn't Captain Lee Min-gu from your class?

40:32.805 --> 40:34.974
I hear he's making Major this round.

40:35.600 --> 40:37.226
You're the poster child
for passed promotions

40:37.310 --> 40:39.145
and you're worried about me?

40:39.604 --> 40:42.357
What? The poster child
for passed promotions?

40:42.440 --> 40:43.441
Me?

40:44.817 --> 40:46.194
What to do?

40:46.527 --> 40:48.655
You'll catch my bad luck
if you work with me. What'll you do?

40:48.738 --> 40:50.573
What is this? Remove it, right now.

40:50.657 --> 40:53.242
Oh my, oh my. I'm the poster child
for passed promotions.

40:53.785 --> 40:55.703
- Right now!
- Okay, so.

40:55.787 --> 40:58.206
What should we be preparing?

40:58.289 --> 40:59.290
Sir?

41:03.169 --> 41:05.463
- The special meal's this summer, right?
- Yes, sir.

41:06.381 --> 41:07.840
Okay, call the battalion supply NCO

41:07.924 --> 41:09.926
and have them send the meal early.

41:10.426 --> 41:11.803
A lot of eyes will be on us

41:11.886 --> 41:13.513
so the presentation must be perfect.

41:13.638 --> 41:16.265
That way, we won't have any of this
'substandard meals' business, right?

41:16.349 --> 41:17.350
Okay.

41:18.017 --> 41:19.477
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
Private Kang Seong-jae

41:19.978 --> 41:20.979
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

41:21.437 --> 41:22.438
Private Kang Seong-jae.

41:22.522 --> 41:25.650
Honestly, the last Pork Cutlet's
presentation was a bit lacking.

41:26.067 --> 41:28.069
This time, make it more fantastic

41:28.152 --> 41:29.821
and delicious, got it?

41:30.947 --> 41:32.323
Got it?

41:37.578 --> 41:40.915
Good grief. All talk, that one.

41:41.582 --> 41:43.292
Hey, you two, over here.

41:50.091 --> 41:52.051
How should we go about choosing the menu?

41:54.887 --> 41:57.473
Let's just do as the Company Commander
said and not get fancy.

41:57.557 --> 41:59.684
Wouldn't it be better
to just play it safe?

41:59.976 --> 42:01.436
We could make ginseng chicken soup

42:01.519 --> 42:03.062
and just toss an abalone in it.

42:03.187 --> 42:05.356
There's nothing better
than that, is there?

42:05.648 --> 42:07.692
That feels like we're just trying
to pull the wool over their eyes.

42:08.192 --> 42:09.736
Everyone on the outside will know.

42:09.819 --> 42:12.780
They'll say we added a special meal
just because a congressman is coming.

42:12.864 --> 42:15.825
Still, we can't exactly serve
what was on the original menu.

42:16.117 --> 42:17.660
Hey, what's on the menu for that day?

42:18.661 --> 42:19.662
That day...

42:19.954 --> 42:21.539
we're scheduled for braised pollack, sir.

42:22.915 --> 42:24.417
Braised pollack?

42:24.500 --> 42:25.501
What?

42:25.585 --> 42:27.462
You mean braised boneless pollack?

42:27.545 --> 42:30.131
Are you kidding me? Of all things,
it has to be braised pollack?

42:30.214 --> 42:33.509
The one dish that everyone throws out
the second they get it...

42:33.593 --> 42:36.471
In my entire military career,
I've never seen a single soul eat it.

42:36.554 --> 42:39.766
You could coat that fish in gold

42:39.849 --> 42:41.309
and you still couldn't save it.

42:41.392 --> 42:42.602
End of discussion! Not happening!

42:42.685 --> 42:44.771
Just take the chicken, the abalone

42:44.854 --> 42:47.815
and use all the year's special meals
and serve them all at once.

42:48.107 --> 42:50.234
Sheesh, forget about the braised pollack!

42:50.318 --> 42:53.154
Yes, Administration &amp; Supply NCO.
This is Park Jae-young.

42:53.237 --> 42:55.323
Oh, man, I heard we're getting
braised pollack that day.

42:55.740 --> 42:58.367
Then, to coincide with
the day of the lecture

42:59.118 --> 43:01.287
I'll arrange for the special meals
to be served early.

43:02.080 --> 43:03.164
All right.

43:03.539 --> 43:04.665
Keep up the good work.

43:04.749 --> 43:05.750
Bye.

43:07.543 --> 43:08.544
Jeez.

43:09.295 --> 43:10.963
- Is it Ganglim?
- Yes.

43:12.340 --> 43:13.800
That Hwang Seok-ho...

43:14.175 --> 43:15.259
Always making things complicated.

43:15.343 --> 43:16.844
He's probably freaking out too.

43:17.220 --> 43:18.221
But...

43:18.721 --> 43:21.182
Can you really expect him to solve
a difficult problem this easily?

43:25.103 --> 43:26.104
NO ENTRY EXCEPT FOR COOKS

43:36.239 --> 43:40.576
AVAILBLE RECIPES: TOFU STEW, PORK CUTLET,
BRAISED BONELESS POLLACK, CHICKEN

43:40.660 --> 43:41.744
AVAILABLE RECIPES
GINSENG CHICKEN SOUP

43:41.828 --> 43:43.079
Here it is.

43:44.080 --> 43:45.414
GINSENG CHICKEN SOUP
SOUP DISH LEVEL 3, CHICKEN DISH LEVEL 3

43:45.498 --> 43:47.500
Currently your proficiency is
Level 2 for Soup Dishes

43:47.583 --> 43:49.794
and Level 2 for Chicken Dishes.

43:49.877 --> 43:51.337
Please increase your proficiency level.

43:52.547 --> 43:54.924
My proficiency level
is just a little too low.

43:58.052 --> 43:59.762
Who's he talking to?

44:10.857 --> 44:12.692
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun's braised chicken.

44:12.775 --> 44:13.776
One star.

44:26.038 --> 44:27.331
ADD CARROTS AND POTATOES

44:27.415 --> 44:29.667
ADDING BLACK BEAN PASTE WILL
INCREASE THE SAVORY FLAVOR

44:32.044 --> 44:34.172
If I add black bean paste to that

44:34.255 --> 44:36.382
it will make it more savory.

44:43.181 --> 44:44.807
- Stop right there.
- It's nothing, sir.

44:44.891 --> 44:46.934
What do you mean? What do you have?

44:47.018 --> 44:48.352
Black bean paste, sir.

44:48.561 --> 44:49.562
Black bean paste?

44:50.271 --> 44:52.273
- We had black bean paste?
- Yes, sir.

44:52.356 --> 44:53.608
Did someone say this would
make it taste better?

44:54.150 --> 44:57.195
Looks like you skimmed some
cooking blog or something.

44:57.320 --> 44:59.405
Mess hall food should be simple.

44:59.572 --> 45:00.740
Don't try to get fancy.

45:00.823 --> 45:02.909
Can't I just try adding
a little bit, please?

45:04.410 --> 45:06.495
Are you telling me to listen to you

45:06.579 --> 45:07.663
because you think my cooking is terrible?

45:07.747 --> 45:08.789
I'm sorry, sir.

45:10.041 --> 45:12.293
You apologizing is just making me angrier.

45:12.376 --> 45:14.795
No, but if you try it with this

45:14.879 --> 45:17.298
you'll notice a difference.

45:22.094 --> 45:23.804
This had better taste good.

45:52.833 --> 45:55.336
Fancy soy-braised chicken. Three stars.

45:55.419 --> 45:58.965
FANCY SOY-BRAISED CHICKEN

46:06.347 --> 46:07.348
Hey.

46:07.431 --> 46:08.432
Private Kang Seong-jae.

46:08.641 --> 46:09.684
Is this it?

46:10.059 --> 46:11.435
Does it taste strange, sir?

46:11.769 --> 46:13.229
It's not that. It's just...

46:13.312 --> 46:15.022
if it's this good

46:15.106 --> 46:17.108
the guys are going to want seconds.

46:18.609 --> 46:19.610
Well, that's a relief.

46:19.694 --> 46:21.279
A relief? If everyone wants seconds

46:21.362 --> 46:22.905
will you take responsibility?

46:25.783 --> 46:26.951
The braised chicken has been completed.

46:27.034 --> 46:29.328
Your proficiency in Chicken Dishes
has increased.

46:29.745 --> 46:32.331
AVAILABLE RECIPE
SOFT TOFU STEW

46:32.415 --> 46:34.125
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.
- What is it?

46:34.375 --> 46:37.003
Let me try my hand
at making the soup today, too.

46:38.587 --> 46:39.588
You sure about that?

46:44.343 --> 46:46.345
I'm not just letting you
because I'm feeling lazy.

46:47.680 --> 46:49.390
Save a few for me. The drumsticks.

46:57.481 --> 47:00.484
Stamina is consumed when you use a recipe.

47:00.568 --> 47:07.575
STAMINA

47:14.206 --> 47:16.125
What kind of nonsense is this?

47:16.917 --> 47:18.669
I thought I made myself clear.

47:18.753 --> 47:21.380
That we serve the special meal early
because the congressman is coming.

47:21.464 --> 47:23.674
But now you're telling me we can't?
What are we supposed to do?

47:24.925 --> 47:27.762
What do you expect us to do now?
Seriously!

47:30.556 --> 47:31.932
Why don't we just tackle this head-on?

47:32.391 --> 47:34.727
Outpost Commander, I'm afraid
the menu for today is...

47:34.935 --> 47:37.521
It's not like we can get our hands
on chicken right now...

47:38.022 --> 47:40.024
Wouldn't this seem more sincere, in a way?

47:40.232 --> 47:43.152
Oh, come on,
Outpost Commander, not you too.

47:43.235 --> 47:44.653
Sincerity, my foot.

47:44.737 --> 47:47.323
The bottom line is, it tastes terrible.

47:47.406 --> 47:49.158
Then isn't there a way

47:49.241 --> 47:50.785
to make the braised pollack taste better?

47:50.868 --> 47:52.453
Come on, if that were possible

47:52.536 --> 47:56.582
why would it always be rated
the worst by active-duty soldiers?

47:59.293 --> 48:00.711
But it's the best we can do

48:00.795 --> 48:02.129
as of right now.

48:02.213 --> 48:03.631
Oh, jeez.

48:07.134 --> 48:08.594
GANGLIM OUTPOST

48:22.691 --> 48:23.692
- Salute!
- Salute!

48:24.026 --> 48:25.361
- Salute!
- At ease.

48:27.822 --> 48:30.032
- I'm Division Commander Kim In-tae.
- Hello.

48:30.574 --> 48:32.410
- Regimental Commander Bae Won-young.
- Hello.

48:32.493 --> 48:34.203
- Battalion Commander Baek Chun-ik.
- Hello.

48:36.038 --> 48:37.706
I'm Congressman Kang Hong-beom.

48:38.207 --> 48:40.876
To all the reporters who came so far

48:40.960 --> 48:42.628
I hope you write some great articles.

48:42.878 --> 48:44.797
Congressman, this way, please.

48:45.214 --> 48:46.215
Wait.

48:46.298 --> 48:48.050
This is my good side.

48:48.259 --> 48:49.260
Oh, yes.

48:52.888 --> 48:54.223
To the congressman, salute!

48:54.306 --> 48:55.433
- Salute!
- Salute!

48:55.891 --> 48:56.892
Salute!

49:07.486 --> 49:08.988
Just looking at them is stressful.

49:09.822 --> 49:11.407
But Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

49:11.866 --> 49:13.325
Why do you hate braised pollack?

49:13.492 --> 49:14.994
It has a terrible fishy smell

49:15.077 --> 49:16.537
and it's dry and flaky when you chew.

49:16.620 --> 49:18.330
I can't even tell what flavor it has.

49:18.539 --> 49:21.625
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
I thought you liked any protein.

49:22.084 --> 49:23.502
I have a weak stomach.

49:24.253 --> 49:25.254
Yeah.

49:26.839 --> 49:30.634
So the key is figuring out how to fix
the fishy smell and the texture.

49:30.718 --> 49:34.388
Jeez, why is the Outpost Commander
making things so difficult?

49:35.931 --> 49:38.309
STAMINA

49:38.642 --> 49:41.353
Using a recipe consumes stamina.

49:41.520 --> 49:43.439
Would you like to use a recipe?

49:49.987 --> 49:51.572
AVAILABLE RECIPE
BRAISED BONELESS POLLACK

49:51.655 --> 49:52.823
SLICE ONIONS AND STIR-FRY IN OLIVE OIL

49:52.907 --> 49:56.535
STAMINA

50:10.424 --> 50:12.009
Guys, we're out of time.

50:12.092 --> 50:13.719
Everyone's heading to the mess hall.

50:13.802 --> 50:15.346
Yes, ma'am.

50:15.429 --> 50:16.805
All right, don't be nervous, okay?

50:16.889 --> 50:17.973
Just relax.

50:18.724 --> 50:22.186
To get rid of the dry texture
of the braised pollack

50:22.269 --> 50:24.939
it's best to fry it until it's crispy.

50:28.359 --> 50:29.360
SEASON THE POLLOCK WITH SALT AND PEPPER
AND ADD COOKING WINE

50:29.443 --> 50:31.487
IN AN OILED PAN OVER MEDIUM-LOW HEAT
PAN-FRY THE POLLOCK UNTIL IT'S CRISPY

50:31.570 --> 50:32.571
IN AN OILED PAN OVER MEDIUM-LOW HEAT
PAN-FRY THE POLLOCK UNTIL IT'S CRISPY

50:32.655 --> 50:34.657
PAN-FRY THE POLLOCK UNTIL IT'S CRISPY

50:38.953 --> 50:44.583
IRONCLAD COASTAL DEFENSE
UNITED THROUGH COMRADESHIP

51:02.017 --> 51:03.477
So? Is it bad?

51:05.854 --> 51:06.855
How is it?

51:08.607 --> 51:09.733
Say something.

51:13.195 --> 51:15.197
I think I managed to fix the texture

51:15.990 --> 51:17.616
but I couldn't remove the fishy smell

51:17.950 --> 51:19.285
from it being frozen.

51:21.620 --> 51:22.621
Hey...

51:23.330 --> 51:24.748
If you can't get rid of the fishy smell

51:25.374 --> 51:26.417
is your military career over?

51:26.709 --> 51:27.835
No, sir.

51:27.918 --> 51:29.670
Do whatever it takes

51:29.753 --> 51:31.672
to get rid of that fishy smell!

51:33.465 --> 51:34.633
Private Kang Seong-jae.

51:34.717 --> 51:35.884
Then I'll check the storeroom

51:35.968 --> 51:39.179
to see if there are any spices
or sauces I can use.

51:51.317 --> 51:52.735
Is it impossible to fix

51:52.818 --> 51:54.945
even if I follow the recipe exactly?

52:10.836 --> 52:13.339
The restaurant smells so fishy.

52:13.422 --> 52:14.423
This stuff...

52:15.299 --> 52:17.051
It's just hard to prepare.

52:17.134 --> 52:19.094
But it's really delicious
once it's cooked.

52:19.178 --> 52:20.846
But the smell is so bad.

52:20.929 --> 52:23.307
Won't you scare away your customers?

52:24.016 --> 52:25.017
Seong-jae.

52:25.225 --> 52:27.186
Hand me that tomato spaghetti sauce.

52:28.812 --> 52:29.813
This?

52:39.073 --> 52:40.532
You're wondering what I'm doing,
aren't you?

52:41.033 --> 52:43.202
- Yeah.
- Just you wait. Okay?

52:50.668 --> 52:53.128
Advanced recipe ingredient acquired.

52:53.379 --> 52:55.089
Using an advanced recipe

52:55.172 --> 52:57.925
will consume one additional stamina.

52:58.217 --> 53:00.010
ADVANCED RECIPE INGREDIENT
CONSUMES EXTRA STAMINA UPON USE

53:00.094 --> 53:01.261
STAMINA

53:03.972 --> 53:06.517
ADVANCED RECIPE INGREDIENT
CONSUMES EXTRA STAMINA UPON USE

53:31.166 --> 53:32.334
- Wait!
- One second!

53:32.418 --> 53:35.671
- Wait... wait...
- Hey, are you crazy?

53:35.754 --> 53:37.381
I told you to get rid of the smell,
not try to kill us...

53:37.464 --> 53:39.508
Is this a suicide mission? Huh?

53:41.176 --> 53:43.721
This is the secret
to getting rid of the smell.

53:52.813 --> 53:55.107
Are you sure this is going to be okay?

53:55.482 --> 53:58.777
- Boneless pollack pasta?
- I think we're screwed.

54:02.072 --> 54:03.449
Salute!

54:04.074 --> 54:05.075
Salute!

54:07.411 --> 54:10.748
It's clear that military life
has improved a lot these days.

54:11.457 --> 54:13.500
Back in my day, 30 of us slept

54:13.834 --> 54:15.377
crammed on sleeping platforms.

54:17.212 --> 54:20.007
Now, the soldiers can serve
in a comfortable environment.

54:20.090 --> 54:22.843
In fact, some soldiers say
it's more comfortable here than home.

54:25.137 --> 54:26.263
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

54:26.346 --> 54:27.848
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol, sir!

54:27.931 --> 54:29.516
So, is military life really
more comfortable than being at home?

54:29.600 --> 54:31.143
- Yes, sir.
- Oh, come on.

54:31.810 --> 54:34.104
Don't give me that textbook answer.

54:34.188 --> 54:35.647
Why do you think I came
all the way out here?

54:36.148 --> 54:37.691
I came to hear firsthand

54:37.775 --> 54:39.401
about the problems that come

54:39.485 --> 54:40.986
with a closed organization
like the military.

54:41.987 --> 54:45.324
My wish is that the soldiers here
finish their service in good health.

54:47.701 --> 54:49.495
You've trained him well.

54:50.579 --> 54:51.663
All right.

54:51.747 --> 54:53.290
Since the reporters are here

54:53.916 --> 54:55.584
along with the Division Commander

54:55.667 --> 54:58.504
and all our soldiers,
I have something to say.

55:00.130 --> 55:03.133
Because of the recent controversy
over poor-quality meals

55:03.217 --> 55:06.261
I came here today
to listen to your voices directly.

55:06.929 --> 55:08.639
In this day and age

55:09.348 --> 55:11.475
how can there be an issue
with our military's meals

55:11.725 --> 55:14.019
when they should be a top priority
for our national defense!

55:14.812 --> 55:16.897
I'm going to see for myself

55:17.648 --> 55:20.901
and make sure that this
never happens again.

55:21.568 --> 55:22.778
Which way is to the mess hall?

55:23.237 --> 55:24.363
This way, sir.

55:26.782 --> 55:27.991
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol, sir!

55:28.242 --> 55:29.243
Let's go eat.

55:31.119 --> 55:32.120
This way, sir.

55:35.666 --> 55:37.084
What did you prepare for the meal?

55:37.626 --> 55:39.670
Don't worry, I talked to them
and made sure they got it.

55:39.753 --> 55:42.297
It's set for this month's special,
ginseng chicken soup.

55:42.381 --> 55:43.590
Okay, good job.

55:43.674 --> 55:46.093
The congressman will enjoy the chicken

55:46.176 --> 55:47.302
so don't you worry.

55:47.469 --> 55:48.470
Yes, sir.

55:55.352 --> 55:57.062
It's okay. Don't worry.

55:58.188 --> 56:00.232
Outpost Commander,
you seem more nervous than any of us.

56:03.610 --> 56:05.195
What's wrong? Are you okay?

56:06.321 --> 56:08.156
I'm fine, ma'am. I think I'm just nervous.

56:08.574 --> 56:11.410
Jeez, why am I the one shaking?
We're just feeding a congressman.

56:11.994 --> 56:13.787
- Here they come.
- They're coming!

56:18.041 --> 56:19.042
Salute!

56:20.043 --> 56:21.044
Right.

56:23.505 --> 56:24.506
Salute!

56:27.050 --> 56:28.051
Please enjoy your meal.

56:29.595 --> 56:31.972
- Master Sergeant Park Jae-young.
- Master Sergeant Park Jae-young, sir.

56:32.055 --> 56:33.056
A pleasure to meet you.

56:33.223 --> 56:34.308
Congressman, I'm a huge fan.

56:34.391 --> 56:35.434
Oh, is that right?

56:37.769 --> 56:38.937
Please enjoy your meal.

56:39.021 --> 56:40.230
Master Sergeant Park Jae-young.

56:44.026 --> 56:45.319
What is this?

56:45.402 --> 56:46.653
What the hell...

56:47.362 --> 56:49.239
What happened?
What about ginseng chicken soup?

56:52.659 --> 56:53.827
That's what I was told.

56:54.036 --> 56:56.872
The congressman hates fishy food.
And you serve him pollack?

56:57.873 --> 56:59.917
Goodness, we'll talk about this later.

57:06.548 --> 57:07.549
Wait.

57:08.425 --> 57:10.135
What... What is this?

57:10.969 --> 57:12.846
It's pomodoro braised
boneless pollack, sir.

57:13.847 --> 57:16.516
- Pomodoro?
- Pomodoro is the Italian word for

57:17.017 --> 57:18.352
tomato.

57:18.435 --> 57:20.103
To address the fishy smell

57:20.187 --> 57:22.147
and texture issues of frozen pollack

57:22.356 --> 57:24.066
I've incorporated a tomato sauce.

57:24.608 --> 57:26.610
The acidic compounds in tomatoes

57:26.693 --> 57:29.279
are effective at neutralizing amines

57:29.363 --> 57:30.739
that cause a fishy odor.

57:38.372 --> 57:40.332
Well, soldiers these days...

57:40.415 --> 57:43.085
are served quite a variety of food.

57:43.961 --> 57:45.921
- Po... what?
- Pomodoro.

57:46.171 --> 57:47.339
Anyway

57:47.422 --> 57:49.174
when it comes to military meals

57:49.675 --> 57:52.344
you can't please everyone's palate

57:53.804 --> 57:55.138
but that doesn't mean...

57:56.223 --> 57:58.141
they should be lacking in any way.

57:58.517 --> 57:59.559
Of course.

58:10.112 --> 58:12.614
Who said to change the menu?
What happened to the ginseng chicken soup?

58:12.698 --> 58:14.199
Is it not to your liking?

58:14.282 --> 58:15.826
It's more original
than ginseng chicken soup.

58:15.909 --> 58:17.244
That's only for special occasions.

58:17.327 --> 58:18.870
But why?

58:19.121 --> 58:21.373
This isn't a game.
Pomodoro, Pororo, whatever...

58:21.456 --> 58:22.666
Why didn't you do as you were told?

58:23.458 --> 58:24.626
Can't you read the room?

58:24.710 --> 58:27.295
Officers are picky. What will you do?

58:28.338 --> 58:30.257
Warning. Stamina is low.

58:30.340 --> 58:31.842
Rest immediately.

58:32.175 --> 58:33.260
No.

58:33.343 --> 58:34.886
- I have to hang on a little longer.
- How much time do you have left?

58:34.970 --> 58:36.638
- Just a little longer.
- Kang Seong-jae.

58:36.972 --> 58:38.056
Private Kang Seong-jae.

58:38.140 --> 58:39.683
I think we need to get more rice.

58:39.975 --> 58:40.976
Yes, I understand.

58:52.696 --> 58:53.697
System.

58:53.780 --> 58:55.782
System overload.

58:55.866 --> 58:58.201
Shutting down system.

59:22.726 --> 59:25.437
SPECIAL THANKS TO
PARK MYUNG-HUN AND KANG GIL-WOO

59:45.749 --> 59:48.668
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

59:48.919 --> 59:49.920
Hey, Kang Seong-jae.

59:50.003 --> 59:51.004
Kang Seong-jae!

59:51.088 --> 59:54.091
How could you be so confident
not knowing about this problem?

59:54.674 --> 59:56.760
If you insisted on doing this,
you should see it through to the end.

59:57.177 --> 59:58.303
Don't just cut corners

59:58.386 --> 01:00:00.514
- and try to muddle through.
- Private Kang Seong-jae!

01:00:00.764 --> 01:00:02.349
Because of all the visitors
for Kang Seong-jae

01:00:02.432 --> 01:00:03.850
I can't get any rest, damn it.

01:00:03.934 --> 01:00:05.227
Hey, I said I'd do it.

01:00:05.310 --> 01:00:08.271
I guess the praise made you greedy

01:00:08.563 --> 01:00:09.773
but our primary enemy...

01:00:10.565 --> 01:00:11.566
is the officers.

01:00:11.858 --> 01:00:13.360
I'm thinking of bringing
Private Kang Seong-jae

01:00:13.860 --> 01:00:15.487
over to the Officers' Mess.

01:00:15.695 --> 01:00:17.280
What's different about the Officers' Mess?
